The paper’s native colouring witnesses satisfy G and V, but not H:

- Track A lacks a hardness result for the generated distribution; the paper instead gives constructive colouring reductions in its low-treewidth/high-degree regime.
- Track B prototypes were either solved by greedy colouring or by the obvious Latin-square/translation ansatz. In the tightest case, the generic method took 2,703–2,991 operations versus 268 for the shortcut, with 252 of those operations needed merely to emit the answer.

The full analysis, theorem references, measured prototypes, and rejected alternatives are in [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1311.2969/REJECTED.md). It is grounded in the [source paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1311.2969) and its cited [fixed-parameter algorithmic context](https://arxiv.org/abs/1110.4077). No oracle calls were spent after H failed.
